        "hypothesis": "A workload-based combination should outperform a full-grid baseline: sparse first-hit counting avoids scanning the grid when there are few unique obstacles, while large non-sparse OpenMP workloads use a tiled wavefront; a linear-memory rolling DP remains the fallback.",
        "id": "93b04c736a2946b3",
